---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '@/components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '@/components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Us | DevCult"
  description="DevCult is a DevEx consultancy for blockchain ecosystems. We run hackathons, fix onboarding, and build DevRel programs that produce measurable developer adoption."
>
  <Header />

  <main id="main-content" class="py-12">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6">
      <h1 data-animate class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold font-coconat">
        We fix what turns developers away from blockchains
      </h1>
      <p data-animate data-delay="100" class="mt-6 text-lg text-text-secondary max-w-3xl">
        Most blockchain ecosystems lose developers in the first 30 minutes. Broken tutorials.
        Confusing architecture diagrams. Documentation written for people who already understand the
        system. We've seen it everywhere. We fix it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Who We Are -->
    <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 mt-20 mb-20">
      <div
        data-animate
        class="p-8 md:p-12 rounded-xl bg-brand-alpha-5 border border-brand-500 border-l-4"
      >
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold font-coconat text-text-primary mb-6">
          Who We Are
        </h2>
        <p class="text-lg text-text-primary mb-4">
          DevCult started because we kept watching the same pattern: brilliant protocol teams shipping
          incredible technology, then wondering why developers weren't showing up.
        </p>
        <p class="text-lg text-text-primary mb-4">
          The answer was almost never the tech. It was the experience around it. Onboarding that assumed
          too much. Events that generated swag photos but not commits. Documentation that explained
          everything except how to make it work.
        </p>
        <p class="text-lg text-text-primary">
          We're a small team that's been inside these problems — at world-class hackathons. Now we help
          ecosystems build the developer experience that fits their technology.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
